    ['Archive QPs and matching MSs','The searchable index includes 23 4EB1 QP and 23 matching MS text records; 23 local QP PDFs, 23 local MS PDFs and two June 2023 ER PDFs are present. The single full PDF collection ZIP is absent.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/ plus Paperlords_Searchable_Text_Index.zip and Paperlords_QP_MS_ER_Pairings.csv.','Use local PDFs for page-image verification; linked online report text is locator evidence only and does not establish candidate wording or unpinned response pages.'],
    ['Pearson June 2019 P1 examiner report, 4EB1_01_1906_ER','Eleven locator-only records across Q3/Q6/Q7/Q8/Q9/Q10/Q11: six Section A, two Q8 and three Section C. All five official text chunks were re-reviewed on 2026-10-28. The first Examoo text chunk confirmed the report title/publication code but no visual page; a same-title 52-page Scribd listing exposed scrambled OCR and its direct page-image route failed; targeted image searches were unrelated. No visual script facsimile or candidate-response page range was obtained, and no wording was transcribed.','Report not local; matching QP/MS PDFs are local under May-June_2019.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20190822.pdf'],
    ['Pearson June 2019 P1R examiner report','Identified on 28 October 2026 as a commentary-only Principal Examiner Feedback report (14 printed pages): it reproduces no candidate scripts for any question, so this paper has no score-bearing exemplar to locate at all. Its Q8 commentary was read in full and is used as examiner guidance in the Q8 answer set (first bullet most often skipped; the letter must not become “too formal given the audience was a friend” and must not read like a recruitment leaflet; a few candidates copied chunks of the extracts). The extracted publication-code line omits “R” despite the official P1R URL/title; no visual report cover was obtained, so the discrepancy remains unresolved.','Report not local; matching P1R QP/MS are local. Scribd listing: https://www.scribd.com/document/479296015/4EB1-01R-pef-20190822. See Answer_Sets/June_2019_P1R_Section_A.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01R_pef_20190822.pdf'],
    ['Pearson official English Language B exemplar booklet','Reviewed all three text chunks while seeking authentic responses for June 2019 P1R and January 2020 P1/P1R. The real student examples use Sample Assessment Materials and New York/Dover tasks, not the June 2019 P1R social-change passages, January 2020 P1 art texts or January 2020 P1R friendship texts; they are not candidate evidence for these papers.','Online Pearson booklet; see the June 2019 P1R and January 2020 P1/P1R answer sets plus Official_Pearson_Exemplar_Index.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/Teaching%20and%20learning%20materials/international-gcse-english-lang-b-exemplar-booklet.pdf'],
    ['Pearson English Language B Answers 1 DOCX','Student-book activity answers and possible responses, not Pearson-reproduced candidate examination scripts; excluded as evidence for June 2019 P1R.','Online Pearson answer resource; see Answer_Sets/June_2019_P1R_Section_A.md.','https://www.pearson.com/content/dam/one-dot-com/one-dot-com/international-schools/pdfs/IGAnswers/IGCSE/IGCSE-English/English-Language-B-Answers-1.docx'],
    ['Pearson January 2020 P1 examiner report, 4EB1_01_2001_PEF','All five text chunks reviewed; no score-bearing candidate-script example located.','Report not local.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20200305.pdf'],
    ['Pearson January 2020 P1R examiner report, 4EB1_01R_2001_PEF','All three returned text chunks were reviewed, including the 28 October 2026 recheck; general examiner commentary only, no score-bearing candidate script or usable Q1–Q7 locator.','Report not local.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01R_pef_20200305.pdf'],
    ['Pearson November 2020 combined P1/P1R report, 4EB1_01_2011_ER','All five text chunks reviewed; no score-bearing candidate-script example located.','Report not local.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20210211.pdf'],
    ['Pearson November 2021 P1 examiner report, 4EB1_01_2111_ER','All five text chunks were reviewed; no score-bearing candidate-script locator was found in that route. This is route-limited, not an absence claim; see the November 2021 answer set.','Report not local.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20220224.pdf'],
    ['November 2021 P1 QP/source and matching official Results MS','Local QP cover confirms 4EB1/01 and log P65895RA. Q1–Q7 prompts, appended Text One/Two and matching Results MS publication code 4EB1_01_2111_MS were visually checked; page map is in the answer set.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/November_2021/; see Answer_Sets/November_2021_P1_Section_A.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4eb1-01-rms-20220224.pdf'],
    ['Pearson January 2022 P1 examiner report, 4EB1_01_2201_ER','All five text chunks reviewed; no score-bearing candidate-script example located.','Report not local.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20220303.pdf'],
    ['Pearson January 2022 P1R examiner report, 4EB1_01R_2201_ER','All three text chunks reviewed; no score-bearing candidate-script example located.','Report not local.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01R_pef_20220303.pdf'],
    ['January 2022 P1 QP/source and matching Results MS audit','The local QP cover confirms 4EB1/01 and log P66374A; matching Results MS identifier 4EB1_01_2201_MS. Q1–Q7 prompts, Text One/Two, blank pages/credits and relevant MS pages were visually checked. Printed MS map: Q1–Q2 p. 4; Q3 indicative/AO2 grid pp. 5–6; Q4–Q5 p. 7; Q6 indicative/AO2 grid pp. 8–9; Q7 indicative p. 10 and comparison/AO3 grid p. 11. The P1 examiner report’s five chunks had been reviewed before this batch; no score-bearing script locator was found in that route, the search was not repeated, and no authentic response was added.','See Answer_Sets/January_2022_P1_Section_A.md; local QP/MS under Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/January_2022/.',''],
    ['January 2022 P1R QP/source and matching Results MS audit','The local P1R QP cover confirms 4EB1/01R and log P66375A; matching Results MS identifier 4EB1_01R_2201_MS. Q1–Q7 prompts, Text One/Two, blank pages/credits and relevant MS pages were rendered and visually checked. Printed MS map: Q1–Q2 p. 4; Q3 indicative/AO2 grid pp. 5–6; Q4–Q5 p. 7; Q6 indicative/AO2 grid pp. 8–9; Q7 indicative p. 10, comparison points p. 11 and AO3 grid p. 12. The P1R examiner report’s three text chunks had been reviewed earlier; no score-bearing candidate-script example was located in that route, the search was not repeated, and no authentic response was added.','See Answer_Sets/January_2022_P1R_Section_A.md; local QP/MS under Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/January_2022/.',''],
    ['June 2023 P1 Q8 QP/source/MS and authentic-response audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01 QP p. 15 (barcode P72858A); appended Source Booklet has Text One printed pp. 2–4 / QP PDF pp. 30–32 and Text Two pp. 5–6 / PDF pp. 33–34. Matching Results MS publication code is 4EB1_01_2306_MS (Paper 01; QP log P72858); Q8 indicative content is p. 13 and AO1/AO4/AO5 grids pp. 14–16. The existing full authentic response is transcribed from ER pp. 36–39; published judgement p. 40 gives 30/30 (AO1 10/10 L5, AO4 12/12 L5, AO5 8/8 L5). The matching MS p. 16 lists AO5 Levels 1–4 only, with 7–8 at Level 4; preserve this unresolved ER/MS label discrepancy without changing the published score.','See Answer_Sets/June_2023_P1_Q8_Section_B.md and Verified_Candidate_Responses/June_2023_Section_A.md; local QP/MS/ER under Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2023/.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International-GCSE/English-Language-B/2016/Exam-materials/4eb1-01-pef-20230824.pdf'],
    ['June 2023 P1R Q8 QP/source/MS and authentic-response audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01R QP p. 15 (barcode P72859A); appended Source Booklet has Text One printed pp. 2–3 / QP PDF pp. 30–31 and Text Two pp. 4–5 / PDF pp. 32–33. Matching P1R Results MS publication code is 4EB1_01R_2306_MS (Paper 01R; QP log P72859); Q8 indicative content is p. 13 and AO1/AO4/AO5 grids pp. 14–16. Pearson’s full response and judgement are on ER pp. 30–34; p. 34 begins with the continuation of the p. 33 final “The” and contains the completed conclusion above the 26/30 judgement (AO1 9/10 L5, AO4 10/12 L4, AO5 7/8 L4). The transcript was corrected after visual review of p. 34; no new authentic-response record was added.','See Answer_Sets/June_2023_P1R_Q8_Section_B.md and Verified_Candidate_Responses/June_2023_Section_A.md; local QP/MS/ER under Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2023/.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International-GCSE/English-Language-B/2016/Exam-materials/4eb1-01r-pef-20230824.pdf'],
    ['June 2023 P1R Q11 QP/MS and authentic-response audit','Exact Q11 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01R QP p. 21; matching Results MS publication code 4EB1_01R_2306_MS (Paper 01R) gives role-model indicative content on p. 17 and the AO4/AO5 grids on pp. 18–19. Pearson’s Walt Disney description runs across ER pp. 53–55 (the printed line “This is a successful response to Question 11.” sits above it on p. 53) with the judgement on p. 56 (26/30; AO4 17/20 Level 5, AO5 9/10 Level 5) and the examiner note on p. 57. The transcript was re-read from rendered crops and its struck words and grammar slips retained; no new authentic-response record was added.','See Answer_Sets/June_2023_P1R_Q11_Section_C.md and Verified_Candidate_Responses/June_2023_Section_A.md; local QP/MS/ER under Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2023/.',''],
    ['June 2023 P1R Q10 QP/MS and authentic-response audit','Exact Q10 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01R QP p. 21; matching Results MS publication code 4EB1_01R_2306_MS (Paper 01R) states on p. 17 that no indicative content can be specified, and the AO4/AO5 grids are pp. 18–19. Pearson’s story runs across ER pp. 47–49 with the judgement on p. 50: 30/30, AO4 20/20 Level 5 and AO5 10/10 Level 5. Printed pp. 45–46 are the Q10/examiner AO5 commentary, not script; the transcript was re-read from rendered crops of pp. 47–49 and its revised opening/closing readings marked. No new authentic-response record was added.','See Answer_Sets/June_2023_P1R_Q10_Section_C.md and Verified_Candidate_Responses/June_2023_Section_A.md; local QP/MS/ER under Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2023/.',''],
    ['June 2023 P1R Q9 QP/MS and authentic-response audit','Exact Q9 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01R QP p. 21 (barcode P72859A02128), with the Section C rubric and 30-mark tariff. Matching Results MS publication code is 4EB1_01R_2306_MS (Paper 01R); Q9 indicative content is p. 17 and the AO4/AO5 grids are pp. 18–19. Pearson’s reproduced script runs across ER pp. 40–43 with the judgement on p. 44: 17/30, AO4 11/20 Level 3 and AO5 6/10 Level 3. The transcript was re-checked against rendered crops of all four script pages and corrected (“As I once Mansa Musa exclaimed”, “such as planet” plus an unclear stroke, “an ave person”, “paniced”, “inorder”, struck-word records); no new authentic-response record was added.','See Answer_Sets/June_2023_P1R_Q9_Section_C.md and Verified_Candidate_Responses/June_2023_Section_A.md; local QP/MS/ER under Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2023/.',''],
    ['May/June 2019 P1 Q8 QP/source/MS and report audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01 QP printed p. 15 (PDF index 14; barcode P58477A), with the Section B rubric “You should spend 1 hour on this section” and the 30-mark tariff. The Extracts Booklet is appended to the same QP PDF: booklet cover printed p. 1 / index 28, Text One printed pp. 2–3 / indices 29–30 and Text Two printed pp. 4–5 / indices 31–32. Matching MS publication code is 4EB1_01_1906_MS; Q8 indicative content is p. 12, AO1 grid p. 13, AO4 grid p. 14 and the AO5 grid p. 15, whose highest band is Level 4 (7–8); Section B totals 30 = AO1 10 + AO4 12 + AO5 8. The June 2019 P1 report text route supplies Q8 commentary (including the Level 3 cap when the first bullet is omitted) and printed judgements for the two authentic Q8 responses (30/30 on p. 29; 15/30 on p. 32), but no facsimile or candidate-script page span, so both stay locator-only and no candidate wording is transcribed from OCR. The answer set is a labelled constructed MS/ER-guided model with accepted alternatives and a bullet-to-source evidence map.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2019/; see Answer_Sets/June_2019_P1_Q8_Section_B.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20190822.pdf'],
    ['May/June 2019 P1R Q8 QP/source/MS and report audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01R QP printed p. 15 (PDF index 14; barcode P59775A) with the Section B rubric and 30-mark tariff. The Extracts Booklet is appended to the same QP PDF: Text One printed pp. 2–4 / indices 29–31, printed p. 5 blank, Text Two printed pp. 6–7 / indices 33–34, printed p. 8 blank. Matching MS Publications Code is 4EB1_01R_1906_MS (printed p. 2); Q8 indicative content is p. 12, AO1 p. 13, AO4 p. 14 and AO5 p. 15, whose highest band is Level 4 (7–8); Section B totals 30 = AO1 10 + AO4 12 + AO5 8. The Summer 2019 Paper 01R report is a Principal Examiner Feedback document: it gives substantive Q8 commentary but reproduces no candidate scripts for any question, so no authentic Q8 response can be located or transcribed for this paper — a structural absence, not an access gap. Its printed code 4EB1_01_1906_ER omits the “R” and remains unresolved (no visual cover). The Examoo P1R mirror path (.../edexcel-b/1r/19-jun/rep.pdf) returns AccessDenied. The answer set is a labelled constructed MS/ER-guided model with accepted alternatives and a bullet-to-source evidence map.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2019/; see Answer_Sets/June_2019_P1R_Q8_Section_B.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01R_pef_20190822.pdf'],
    ['January 2020 P1 Q8 QP/source/MS and report audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01 QP printed p. 15 (PDF index 14; barcode P59776A; cover “Paper Reference 4EB1/01”, 14 January 2020) with the Section B rubric and 30-mark tariff. The Extracts Booklet is appended to the same QP PDF: Text One printed pp. 2–3 / indices 29–30, Text Two printed pp. 4–5 / indices 31–32 (with the Picasso/Dora Maar plate), printed pp. 6–8 blank. Matching MS Publications Code is 4EB1_01_2001_MS; Q8 indicative content is p. 11, AO1 p. 12, AO4 p. 13 and AO5 p. 14, whose highest band is Level 4 (7–8); Section B totals 30 = AO1 10 + AO4 12 + AO5 8. The January 2020 P1 report reproduces no candidate script for Q8 or any other question, so no authentic Q8 response can be located or transcribed — a structural absence, not an access gap. Its Q8 guidance is applied in the answer set: the “different types of art” bullet was “sometimes less developed… candidates tending to list the different types with no additional development”; “a significant number of candidates lifted information from the texts especially whole sentences”; addresses “are not necessary”; and letters were “rather too formal for a letter to a friend”. The answer set is a labelled constructed MS/ER-guided model with accepted alternatives and a bullet-to-source evidence map.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/January_2020/; see Answer_Sets/January_2020_P1_Q8_Section_B.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20200305.pdf'],
    ['January 2020 P1R Q8 QP/source/MS and report audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01R QP printed p. 15 (PDF index 14; barcode P60320A; cover “Paper Reference 4EB1/01R”, 14 January 2020): write an article for a school or college website titled ‘Friendship’ — the first article-form Q8 in the archived series. The Extracts Booklet is appended to the same QP PDF: Text One printed pp. 2–3 / indices 29–30, Text Two printed pp. 4–5 / indices 31–32, printed pp. 6–8 blank. Matching MS Publications Code is 4EB1_01R_2001_MS; that mark scheme prints NO page numbers, so Q8 indicative content is cited as PDF p. 13 (index 12, also checked as a rendered page image) and the AO1/AO4/AO5 grids as PDF pp. 14–16 (indices 13–15); AO1 runs to 9–10, AO4 to 11–12 and AO5 stops at Level 4 (7–8). Section B totals 30 = AO1 10 + AO4 12 + AO5 8. The January 2020 P1R report reproduces no candidate script for any question — a structural absence, not an access gap — but its Q8 commentary is used as guidance: candidates needed “the appropriate register for an article for a school or college website”; “many answers were quite similar to one another”; more able candidates “added their own feelings, opinions and experiences”; less able candidates “directly lifted much material from the source texts”. The answer set is a labelled constructed MS/ER-guided article with accepted alternatives and a bullet-to-source evidence map.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/January_2020/; see Answer_Sets/January_2020_P1R_Q8_Section_B.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01R_pef_20200305.pdf'],
    ['May/June/November 2020 P1 Q8 QP/source/MS and report audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01 QP printed p. 15 (PDF index 14; barcode P63884A; cover “Paper Reference 4EB1/01”, dated 2 June 2020): “You have been asked to give a talk to your peers about how to cope with losing important items. Write the text of your talk.” — the first spoken-form Q8 in the archived series. The Extracts Booklet is appended: Text One printed pp. 2–3 / indices 29–30 (Marian Keyes), Text Two printed pp. 4–6 / indices 31–33 (Christopher Mele), printed p. 7 blank and credits on printed p. 8. Matching MS Publications Code is 4EB1_01_2011_MS; Q8 indicative content is printed p. 11, AO1 p. 12, AO4 p. 13 and AO5 p. 14, whose highest band is Level 4 (7–8); Section B totals 30 = AO1 10 + AO4 12 + AO5 8. The combined November 2020 report reproduces no candidate script for any question, so no authentic Q8 response can be located or transcribed. Its 4EB1/01 Q8 guidance is applied in the answer set: the first bullet “was sometimes less developed… candidates tending to list the different items with no additional development”; “candidates lost the register of a talk after a lively introduction”; subheadings left the form unclear; punctuation was the common AO5 weakness. The answer set is a labelled constructed MS/ER-guided talk with accepted alternatives and a bullet-to-source evidence map.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June-November_2020/; see Answer_Sets/MayJuneNov_2020_P1_Q8_Section_B.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20210211.pdf'],
    ['May/June/November 2020 P1R Q8 QP/source/MS and report audit','Exact Q8 prompt is on the local 4EB1/01R QP printed p. 15 (PDF index 14; barcode P62600A; cover “Paper Reference 4EB1/01R”, dated 2 June 2020): an educational website asks for contributions on extreme weather and its effect on the landscape and people. The Extracts Booklet is appended: Text One printed pp. 2–3 / indices 29–30 (Kelsie Knowles), Text Two printed pp. 4–5 / indices 31–32 (Katy Gardner), printed pp. 6–7 blank and credits on printed p. 8. Matching MS Publications Code is 4EB1_01R_2011_MS; Q8 indicative content is printed p. 11, AO1 p. 12, AO4 p. 13 and AO5 p. 14, whose highest band is Level 4 (7–8); Section B totals 30 = AO1 10 + AO4 12 + AO5 8. The combined November 2020 report reproduces no candidate script for any question, so no authentic Q8 response can be located or transcribed. Its 4EB1/01R Q8 guidance is applied in the answer set: candidates must not treat the task as “climate change alone”; weaker answers “only focused on one bullet point, generally the first”; “purpose was the weakest” and “some responses were more essay-like and formal”; article omission was the common AO5 slip. The 4EB1/01 section of the same report covers a different Q8 task and is not used as evidence here. The answer set is a labelled constructed MS/ER-guided website contribution with accepted alternatives and a bullet-to-source evidence map.','Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June-November_2020/; see Answer_Sets/MayJuneNov_2020_P1R_Q8_Section_B.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_pef_20210211.pdf'],
    ['Next selected answer-set batch','All 23 indexed QP/MS pairs have complete Section A Q1–Q7 sets. June 2023 P1 is now complete at 11/11, with Q8 (30/30) and Q9–Q11 (17/30, 30/30 and 23/30) taken from already indexed authentic scripts; P1R Q8 (26/30), P1R Q9 (17/30), P1R Q10 (30/30) and P1R Q11 (26/30) are also complete, so both June 2023 papers stand at 11 of 11. Six Section B Q8 sets are now complete as constructed MS/ER-guided answers (May/June 2019 P1 and P1R, January 2020 P1 and P1R, May/June/November 2020 P1 and P1R), each at QP p. 15 with Section B = AO1 10 + AO4 12 + AO5 8. Three are non-letter forms whose AO4 work is not interchangeable with the letter sets: January 2020 P1R asks for an article (‘Friendship’, school or college website), May/June/November 2020 P1 asks for the text of a talk to peers, and May/June/November 2020 P1R asks for a contribution to an educational website about extreme weather. The June 2019 P1 paper’s two authentic Q8 responses stay locator-only; the June 2019 P1R, January 2020 P1/P1R and November 2020 combined reports reproduce no candidate scripts at all. Next, continue the Section B Q8 series with May/June 2021 P1 Q8: verify the exact QP/source and matching MS, then build the answer and record accepted alternatives.','See Verified_Candidate_Responses/June_2023_Section_A.md and Answer_Sets/README.md.',''],
    ['Pearson May/June 2021 P1 optional unseen-assessment source and public-response gap','Pearson confirms the planned May/June exams did not go ahead as normal and that this QP was optional unseen assessment material for teacher-assessed grades. Guidance allowed centres to self-mark or use Pearson’s optional marking service; the public final Results MS accounts for actual responses but does not identify or publish an individual script. The final scheme and local provisional copy share QP log P65894A and publication code 4EB1_01_2106_MS; relevant Q1–Q7 material was reviewed in both, but no complete line-by-line diff is claimed. Exact-code/barcode/source-title searches and the dynamic course-materials route found no public score-bearing response or examiner report for this QP. The secure Overview Document redirects to Pearson sign-in and was not accessed. This is a public-source gap, not evidence that no centre-held or Pearson-marked unseen response exists; such work is not a normal live-exam script.','Local QP and provisional MS are in Paperlords_Archive/IGCSE/4EB1_English_Language_B/May-June_2021/; see Answer_Sets/MayJune_2021_P1_Section_A.md and Source_Notes/Official_Pearson_Exemplar_Index.md.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/en/qualifications/edexcel-international-gcses/international-gcse-english-language-b-2016/summer-2021-support.html ; https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/Support/DD02688_Customer_Facing_Asset_V2g.pdf ; https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_rms_20210604.pdf ; https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International%20GCSE/English%20Language%20B/2016/exam-materials/4EB1_01_msc_20210517.pdf ; https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/secure/silver/all-uk-and-international/international-gcse/english-language-b/2016/teaching-and-learning-materials/4EB1-IG-English-Language-B-Overview-Document.pdf ; https://qualifications.pearson.com/en/qualifications/edexcel-international-gcses/international-gcse-english-language-b-2016.coursematerials.html'],
    ['Pearson November 2023 P1 examiner report, 4EB1_01_ER_2311','All five text chunks reviewed; no score-bearing candidate-script example located. The official report is linked online but is not present in the local archive.','Report not local; the local November 2023 P1 QP/MS PDFs are present.','https://qualifications.pearson.com/content/dam/pdf/International-GCSE/English-Language-B/2016/Exam-materials/4eb1-01-pef-20240125.pdf'],
    ['June 2023 Source Booklet text','Separate Source Booklet PDFs are not present; the text is appended to the local QPs: P1 PDF pp. 30–34 (printed pp. 2–6) and P1R PDF pp. 30–33 (printed pp. 2–5). Candidate-script references are not treated as source-verified quotations unless a specific cross-check is recorded.','The local June 2023 P1 and P1R QP PDFs.',''],
